ENGROVE AUDIO LAB | ALIEN LT | K2 GRADED 1 PLY KIT
Engineering construction study. Units are mm. One mirror pair of mouldings.
Read with Wand_K2_Graded_1_Ply_Kit.step (AP242 tessellated named solids).

DATUM    Stylus at (0,0,0), +X rearwards, +Z up. W01 is the negative-Y
         half (L-) and W02 the positive-Y half (R-). Traverse each half
         from the centre of the sole towards its flank and the roof seam.
         s is this 3D meridian's accumulated length. e=s/half-perimeter.
         Both planar end returns close on Y=0. The two halves butt at Y=0.

TOOL     Use the R3 Cobra exterior including the pitch saddle at X237.10,
         Z1.50, axis Y, and the side gauge seats Ø10.16. The frozen K2
         assembly keeps this exterior, front pickup slots and two lead exits.
         K2 assembly SHA-256 (unpacked STEP):
         c30f1f7f300cff19718ec62b6f85071cd351ca0c313e7bb395bbae2e94e77ad6

TEXTILE  B = opened CF-BR-40 braid, paired target directions +45° and −45°.
         U = CF-TP-RB-80-15-10 axial UD, stock width 15. Matrix is WEST SYSTEM
         105/205. Nominal fibre volume fraction 0.50. B is 0.364045 cured,
         U is 0.087912 cured. Check actual angle and cured gauge on the tool.
         Axial is +X projected into each true tangent plane, with the wrap
         continuing onto its planar ends. Positive angle turns from the axial
         direction towards the outward normal cross axial. Reflection swaps
         +45 and −45. Cut the two mirror halves with their own handed marks.

PLACE    Work from tool / outside inwards. Place only the following whole
         material pieces in order: UF, B0, BO, U0, UR, B1F or B1A, BI.
         UF = front replacement axial, B0 = continuous outer base braid,
         BO = aft outer braid, U0 = axial base, UR = aft axial, B1F / B1A
         = inner base braid before / after front replacement, BI = aft inner
         braid. Individual 15-wide U0 courses have s boundaries 0,15,30,...
         UF and UR begin with 7.5, then 22.5,37.5,...; trim outermost course
         to the roof seam. Braid panels are opened. Use close-fitting butt
         edges for the nominal study. Dry cut maps can join pieces separated
         only by a subsequent hole. Inspect the separate 1:1 dry templates.

GRADING  Divide each meridian into four consecutive quarter-perimeter bands.
         Each band has a fixed phase q. From sole to roof:
            UF / BO :  1/8  3/8  5/8  7/8
            UR      :  3/8  5/8  7/8  1/8
            BI      :  5/8  7/8  1/8  3/8
         Place UF from X=27+15q to 158−21q. Outside UF, retain B1F or B1A.
         Place BO, UR and BI from X=170+25q to 295−17q, only at
         hypot(X−286,Y) ≥ 20+7q. Preserve the baseline near the capsule.
         Leave the material as full plies with staggered edges in the tool.
         Full fields from tool into cavity:
            nose/base:     B0 / U0 / B1               0.816002
            light front:   UF / B0 / U0               0.539869
            eligible aft:  B0 / BO / U0 / UR / B1 / BI 1.632004
         The selectable engineering STEP shows a short modelled edge drop
         over 0.85 mm developed distance. A resin/compaction model uses
         local tool directions near corners, contact gauges and tip returns.
         Each 15-mm axial course retains its full nominal gauge at butt seams.

OPENINGS Machine after cure:
         • Pickup slots in the sole. Two stadiums 8.80 × 2.80 in X,Y with
           arc centres (7.20, ±6.35) and (13.20, ±6.35), end radius 1.40.
         • Round-ended X1.50 × Y2.80 lead exits at (40,0) and (226.8,0).
           In the sole near X40, retain base B1F instead of UF within 2+12q
           of the opening edge. Near X226.8 omit extra BO, UR, BI within
           respectively 2, 8 and 14 of the opening edge. Base plies remain.
         • Capsule opening Ø30.20, axis Z at (286,0). Preserve the ring land.
         • Rear lock access Ø3.40, axis X at (Y0,Z−5). The facet envelope
           has 0.0025 radial allowance at this last directly gauged opening.
         Gauge the Ø14.20 saddle and both side seats. Keep screws, slots,
         wire entries and the clockable insert free. The two K2 doublers,
         metal components and local bond films are separate items
         in the study assembly. They are outside the shell-ply kit.

DELIVERY Each receiving CAD product is one named closed tessellated solid.
         Nominal prepreg/laminate gauges and formed intersections are distinct.
         The opened neutral file carries net, trimmed study geometry. Use
         its source register and the full-size cut patterns for fabrication.
         Check end returns, relief, physical fibre angles and fits on dry
         trial material before committing resin. Local compaction, adhesive
         bedding and finishing are not constitutive results of this study.

CHECK    The outer mould and both true, planar end curves are referenced to
         the native K2/R3 CAD. Adjacent offset interfaces agree within
         0.000211 mm at matched vertices. Whole closed-facet checks found
         at most 0.00677 mm on the smaller side of a local facet crossing.
         Near-tangent projected face excursions are reported separately in
         the intersection audit. Form the ends on the tool and trim to the
         real joint, bore and half-seam gauges. Reference CAD is in mm.
